      "answer": "$\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}-\\frac\\pi6\\right)r^2$",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Angle $BAD$, $BAC$ or $CAD=\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$ or $120^\\circ$ — B1 SOI unless associated with the wrong angle; condone 2.09 for this mark only. Sector $BAD=\\frac12r^2\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$ — B1. Sector $BCD=\\frac12s^2\\frac\\pi3$ — B1*. Simplify it using $s=\\sqrt3r$ to $\\frac12\\pi r^2$ — DB1. Either triangle $ABD$, $ABC$ or $ACD$: $\\frac12r^2\\sin\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$ or $\\frac12rs$ — B1*, possibly multiplied by 2 or 3; $\\frac12r^2\\sin\\frac\\pi3=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}r^2$ used for the indicated wrong angle is B0DB0. Simplify to $\\frac{\\sqrt3}{4}r^2$ — DB1. Or triangle $CBD=\\frac12s^2\\sin\\frac\\pi3$ or $\\frac32rs$ — B1*, with $\\frac12s^2\\sin\\frac{2\\pi}{3}=\\frac{3\\sqrt3}{4}r^2$ for the indicated wrong angle scoring B0DB0; simplify to $\\frac{3\\sqrt3}{4}r^2$ — DB1. Fully correct area $\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}-\\frac\\pi6\\right)r^2$, or $\\left(\\frac{12\\sqrt3-4\\pi}{24}\\right)r^2$, in the required exact form — B1. Accept $a=\\sqrt3/2,b=-1/6$. Total 7.",
